{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall set apart every firstling that opens the womb to HaShem</b> — in the manner of the plain interpretation: you shall pass it over from the flock to be for HaShem. And he went back and explained what this passing-over is: every firstling of an animal, the males, and the firstling of a donkey, and the firstborn of man among his children — they shall be for HaShem. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Exodus 13:12), <b>And you shall set apart every firstling that opens the womb to HaShem</b> — the verse speaks of the firstborn of man."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The referent of 'he went back and explained' is uncertain; it likely refers to Rashi, who first glosses the phrase generally and then specifies the categories. Alternatively it may refer to the Torah itself. Translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:24.664880762Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}